[Music]  hello everyone my name is nori and i'm  writing these one to two minute long  pieces for the little keyboard that i  have  this week i wrote a fugue thank you to  eric and rhys for submitting this idea  on instagram  [Music]  first of all here's the subject  [Music]  it almost sounds like a family of  chipmunks  they're going somewhere  this fugue has three voices and i used a  few traditional devices to transform the  subject in different ways  these include the inversion  the retrograde  [Music]  and the retrograde inversion  by the way thank you to everyone who  contributed with an idea for what to  base these pieces on i compiled them in  a list and i'll make sure to go through  as many as i can in the next coming  weeks  [Music]  the challenging part of writing a few is  to have all the different voices  complement each other while maintaining  independence this is also what generally  makes fugu sound complex and layered  [Music]  and now here's the piece  [Music]  do  [Music]  do  [Music]  so i hope you enjoy that thank you so  much for watching and please share with  me any ideas or requests you have for  these little pieces subscribe if you  haven't already and i'll see you in the  next video  [Music]  you

